  "original_source_text": "Function-as-a-Service (FaaS) has become a de-facto paradigm for deploying cloud applications, yet it exposes sensitive data to untrusted infrastructures. Running functions on confidential virtual machines (CVMs) such as Intel TDX provides strong isolation for data but significantly increases cold-start latency due to CVM initialization. This paper presents TDSnap, the first TDX-aware function snapshot system that records a verified function state with its TD and restores it on demand. Using snapshot-bounded attestation and TD-aware working-set identification, TDSnap preserves TDX isolation while reducing cold-start latency. Evaluation shows that TDSnap reduces cold-start latency by up to 40x and matches non-TDX snapshot systems.",
